    <item>
      <title>No. 7 UC Santa Cruz men’s volleyball team upsets No. 3 Cathage in a five-set thriller | College Local Roundup</title>
      <link>https://www.santacruzsentinel.com/2026/02/13/no-7-uc-santa-cruz-mens-volleyball-team-upsets-no-3-cathage-in-a-five-set-thriller-college-local-roundup/</link>
      <description>Riley Norman had 22 kills, including the match winner, eight assists, and seven digs, and the No. 7 nationally ranked NCAA Division III UC Santa Cruz men's volleyball team upset No. 3 Cathage in a five-set thriller, 19-25, 25-22, 23-25, 25-21, 15-13, in Kenosha, Wisconsin, on Friday.</description>
      <guid isPermaLink="false">https://www.santacruzsentinel.com/2026/02/13/no-7-uc-santa-cruz-mens-volleyball-team-upsets-no-3-cathage-in-a-five-set-thriller-college-local-roundup/</guid>
